I wrote the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as fad9065d. The build is green: the harness verified it at session start, and a live -p call returned PONG. All 10 recent sessions were green with no reverts.

What the planner should know:
• Two files are close to failing the size limit in `cargo test`. src/help.rs has 10 lines of room and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs has 14 (it's 36 lines over the cap and not on the exceptions list). A failure there undoes the whole task, so any task touching either file should first update its entry in the size list.
• A new misleading error, with no ticket. yoyo --system --model claude-zzz -p hi now refuses safely: nothing is sent and it exits non-zero. But it blames -p for the stray word. What actually happened is that --system took --model as its value. The error's suggested fix, -p "hi claude-zzz", would send the model name to the model as part of the prompt.
• #1127 isn't finished. In the shell, yoyo docs, yoyo risk zz1 and yoyo memories still print the chat-window slash forms (/docs, /risk, /remember).
• #1094 item 1 needs a decision. Overwriting a file that was never read is still allowed. Claude Code refuses it. yoagent deliberately allows it (tools/file.rs: "this guard is about partial reads only"). That gives a ready comparison for either deciding it or sending @yuanhao a two-option question. The test with "undecided" in its name should be renamed after the behaviour it actually checks.
• Refused runs exit 0. I ran yoyo --deny '*' -p "use bash: echo hi": the command was refused, the model said REFUSED, and yoyo exited 0. Claude Code 2.1.319 changed a similar case to exit 1. Their case is a missing safety check rather than the user's own deny rule, though, so I recorded it as an observation rather than a bug.
• #1149 is still waiting on @yuanhao (whether -p and piped runs should keep approving every tool call). The assessment says not to change that default.

Today's earlier research had already added Claude Code 2.1.319 and Codex CLI 0.167.0 to my knowledge vault, so I added nothing new there. The assessment ends with four suggested picks, in order: #1094 item 1, the #1127 leftovers, the misleading error above, and the size-list fix.
